"use strict";(self.webpackChunk_N_E=self.webpackChunk_N_E||[]).push([[9694],{29694:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"schemaVersion":1,"locale":"en","slug":"09-bank","title":"Lesson 09. The bank on your side: Get more from the bank than it takes from you","sourceFingerprint":"5d46c6a5f8328749cee97a4a9c951e8f5e867a2db805a841c4c55ee4d59daa31","blocks":[{"id":"b001","markdown":"## The bank on your side"},{"id":"b002","markdown":"Get more from the bank than it takes from you"},{"id":"b003","markdown":"The bank earns from you in 2 places. It acquires your money cheaply and lends it dearly: unpaid salary-card balances are put to work. It also lends to you dearly: cards at 50%, consumer loans or instalments with hidden extra cost."},{"id":"b004","markdown":"This lesson reverses the pattern: earn on your own money, and where possible use bank money free. Do not expect riches. Social media loves banking schemes supposedly earning hundreds of thousands annually; real figures are more modest. But it is money most people simply give their bank every month."},{"id":"b005","markdown":"### Money on a card at 0%"},{"id":"b006","markdown":"Working on a banking app quickly teaches which figures matter. A key one is how much clients leave in ordinary cards and accounts where the bank pays almost nothing. The larger the balance, the cheaper the funds it later lends. Salary schemes, convenient card transfers and attractive home-screen balances are not designed without purpose."},{"id":"b007","markdown":"For you, the implication is simple. An average card balance of 100 000 RUB could earn around 13 000 RUB annually in a 13% savings account. The bank certainly does not lose that income. Keep money not needed in the coming days in savings. Transfers between your accounts are instant and free, so access is barely affected."},{"id":"b008","markdown":"### Choosing a savings account"},{"id":"b009","markdown":"#### Daily balance"},{"id":"b010","markdown":"Lesson 6 covered this, but it is central. Interest can use daily balances or the month’s minimum. The second often advertises more, but one mid-month withdrawal forfeits the whole month’s interest on that amount. If you actively use the money, choose daily-balance calculation."},{"id":"b011","markdown":"#### Welcome and base rates"},{"id":"b012","markdown":"Banks attract newcomers with higher introductory rates. According to Finuslugi, early October 2026 offers reached about 15.5% for the first 2 months. Check the rate after those 2 months too. The base is often 1.5–2 times lower: 7–10% instead of 15%."},{"id":"b013","markdown":"You can move money to another bank when an introductory rate ends. It works, but requires tracking dates and terms. Whether a few extra percentage points justify your time is your decision."},{"id":"b014","markdown":"#### Is the rate reasonable?"},{"id":"b015","markdown":"The Bank of Russia publishes a benchmark every 10 days: the average maximum deposit rate at the 10 largest banks. In the second ten-day period of October 2026 it was 13.06%."},{"id":"b016","markdown":"The regulator recommends that banks avoid attracting money far above that benchmark. A much higher rate may indicate urgently needed funding rather than a gift. Check deposit-insurance membership and do not keep more than 1.4 million RUB there."},{"id":"b017","markdown":"Figures at the time of writing"},{"id":"b018","markdown":"Average maximum deposit rate at the 10 largest banks, second ten-day period of October: 13.06%. Text figures are dated to writing. Check current values on the official Bank of Russia website."},{"id":"b019","markdown":"### Fixed deposit or savings account"},{"id":"b020","markdown":"Savings-account money is always accessible, but the bank may lower its rate any day. A deposit locks money for a term but fixes the rate. That distinction matters now. Average maximum rates among the 10 largest banks by term in October 2026, according to the central bank:"},{"id":"b021","markdown":"| Deposit term | Rate |\\n| Up to 90 days | 12.55% |\\n| 91–180 days | 12.87% |\\n| 181 days – 1 year | 12.73% |\\n| Over 1 year | 11.75% |\\nLong deposits pay less because banks expect falling rates and avoid long promises of high interest. Practical implication: money certainly unnecessary for a year may reasonably be fixed in a deposit now. If rates fall, savings-account interest falls but the deposit remains unchanged."},{"id":"b022","markdown":"### Where cashback comes from"},{"id":"b023","markdown":"When you pay by card, the shop pays its bank an acquiring fee, usually 1–2.5% of the purchase. The bank returns some as cashback to encourage use of its card. Cashback is therefore your share of a fee the merchant already paid; it is worth collecting."},{"id":"b024","markdown":"Choose 1–2 cards matching lesson 2’s main expenses, such as groceries, fuel, pharmacies or marketplaces, without excessive effort. Select monthly categories for your spending rather than the largest headline percentage. Never buy for cashback: 10% back on something unnecessary means 90% lost."},{"id":"b025","markdown":"For scale: 60 000 RUB monthly spending with average cashback of 1.5% produces around 10 800 RUB yearly. Useful, but not worth maintaining 8 cards and spending evenings configuring them."},{"id":"b026","markdown":"WHERE CASHBACK COMES FROM. YOU PAY THE SHOP BY CARD. THE SHOP PAYS THE BANK 1–2.5%. PART RETURNS TO YOU. CASHBACK IS YOUR SHARE OF THE MERCHANT’S FEE."},{"id":"b027","markdown":"### What about a credit card?"},{"id":"b028","markdown":"You can use bank money free by paying for purchases by credit card and repaying fully before grace ends, while your own money earns interest in savings. At average spending this adds around 10 000 RUB yearly beyond cashback."},{"id":"b029","markdown":"But it is for people with no debts, a cushion and exceptional discipline. A single late payment at 50% can consume the year’s benefit. It therefore has its own step-by-step supplementary guide: Guide 2, Credit Card Without Interest."},{"id":"b030","markdown":"### Paid bank subscriptions"},{"id":"b031","markdown":"Banks sell subscriptions offering better cashback, balance interest, free transfers or airport lounges. They help only when the benefits you actually use exceed the price."},{"id":"b032","markdown":"Use your own spending. A 400 RUB monthly subscription costs 4 800 RUB yearly; if extra cashback is 2 000 RUB, you lose money. Such subscriptions are often free with a certain balance or spending level. Check the conditions."},{"id":"b033","markdown":"Where does the bank earn from you, and how much can you recover?"},{"id":"b034","markdown":"Balance. Cashback. Subscription. Average card balance: 100 000 RUB. Forgone annual income: 13 100 RUB."},{"id":"b035","markdown":"Annually, if not in a savings account earning 13.1%."},{"id":"b036","markdown":"The bank does not lose it: a card balance at 0% is put to work. Keep funds not needed in the coming days in savings. Rate: the average maximum among the 10 largest banks in Bank of Russia data, second ten-day period of October."},{"id":"b037","markdown":"### Fees you can avoid"},{"id":"b038","markdown":"- Faster Payments System transfers between your own accounts at different banks are free within 30 million RUB monthly."},{"id":"b039","markdown":"- Many banks waive card maintenance fees under simple conditions; check whether you qualify."},{"id":"b040","markdown":"- Paid SMS notifications often duplicate free in-app push notifications."},{"id":"b041","markdown":"- Other banks’ cash machines have free-withdrawal limits."},{"id":"b042","markdown":"### The essentials"},{"id":"b043","markdown":"- Keep spare money in daily-balance savings, not on the card."},{"id":"b044","markdown":"- Use the central bank’s average maximum among the 10 largest banks as a rate benchmark, currently around 13%."},{"id":"b045","markdown":"- Long deposits currently pay less than short ones as the market expects falling rates. Consider fixing money not needed for a year."},{"id":"b046","markdown":"- Cashback is a share of the merchant’s fee: take it, but do not buy for it."},{"id":"b047","markdown":"The module’s final lesson examines money reclaimable from the state. Many leave tens of thousands unclaimed every year."}],"terms":[{"id":"strakhovanie-vkladov","term":"Deposit insurance","definition":"A state guarantee to repay depositors up to a certain amount if a bank fails. In Russia, 1.4 million RUB per bank through the Deposit Insurance Agency."},{"id":"ekvayring","term":"Card acquiring","definition":"The fee of 1.5–3% a shop pays its bank for accepting cards. Some returns to you as cashback; the remainder stays with the bank. That is why banks promote high cashback."}],"quizzes":[{"id":"09-bank-q1","q":"Where does bank cashback money come from?","options":["Bank profits as a gift to customers","Taxes","The fee the shop pays the bank for card acceptance"],"correct":2},{"id":"09-bank-q2","q":"One-year deposit rates are below 3–6-month rates. What does that indicate?","options":["Banks expect lower rates and avoid promising high interest for long","Long deposits are always worse","Banks expect rising inflation"],"correct":0},{"id":"09-bank-q3","q":"A bank offers far above the average maximum rate of the 10 largest banks. What should you do?","options":["Immediately move every saving there","Check deposit-insurance membership and keep no more than 1.4 million RUB there","No check needed: a high rate always means reliability"],"correct":1}],"officialSources":[]}')}}]);